# Negative test: every GMN operator form that declares a gmeow:gmnFixity (infix, prefix,
# postfix, or bracketing) MUST also carry BOTH gmeow:gmnPrecedence and gmeow:gmnArity, so
# #1377's operator-precedence parser always reads a COMPLETE operator signature — fixity,
# binding strength, and operand count together. A form that declares a fixity but omits
# either precedence or arity is a half-specified operator, undecidable from data.
#
# Constant forms (number-space signs like ℕ ℤ ℚ ℝ ℂ, the π/γ constants) carry no fixity
# and are exempt by construction — they name no operator grammar. Distinct forms may
# SHARE a precedence level by design (the additive band 60, the multiplicative band 70
# each hold several forms), so this gate checks only the PRESENCE of a precedence and an
# arity, never their distinctness.
#
# Any returned row is a violation: a fixity-bearing form missing its precedence or arity.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX lang: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/>

SELECT ?form ?fixity WHERE {
    ?form a lang:Form ;
          lang:inSignSystem gmeow:gmnModelNotation ;
          gmeow:gmnFixity ?fixity .
    FILTER (NOT EXISTS { ?form gmeow:gmnPrecedence ?precedence }
            || NOT EXISTS { ?form gmeow:gmnArity ?arity })
}
ORDER BY ?form
